To run it manually:
1) compile nvmesh using build.sh with IM_TEST=yes to compile this test, no must for IM_CLIENT/TARGET/BOTH.
2) sudo insmod ./common_public/nvmeib_common_public.ko.xz  ib_odp_info=`grep -c ib_umem_odp_get /proc/kallsyms 2> /dev/null`
3) sudo insmod ./common_public/nvmeib_common_mlx5_public.ko.xz
4) sudo insmod ./common/nvmeib_common.ko.xz
5) sudo insmod ./testing/pcie_atomic/pcie_atom_test.ko.xz
6) sudo ./testing/pcie_atomic/run.sh mlx5_0:1 mlx5_1:1 5 (or your choosen ports/nics)
7) search for the result line in dmesg
pass example:
[Tue Oct  5 07:54:30 2021] (241715/30)atom_test.c[end_thread_fn](647): Test finished - Runtime: 5 secs Count 1: 6135280 Count 2: 6140704 Total Count: 12275984 Atomic Failure: FALSE
failed example:
[Mon Oct  4 16:42:16 2021] (9675/24)atom_test.c[end_thread_fn](642): Test finished - Runtime: 4 secs Count 1: 16 Count 2: 16 Total Count: 0 Atomic Failure: TRUE
